 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "The adjunction $j_!\\dashv j^*$",
 "statement": "For an open immersion $j\\colon U\\to X$, the extension by zero $j_!$ of\n[def-sfb-finite-extension-by-zero] is left adjoint to the pullback $j^*$ of\n[def-sfb-finite-upper-star]. The pullback is computed by restriction:\n$(j^*G)(T\\to U)\\cong G(T\\to U\\to X)$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-six-functors-basics/sk-def-sfb-finite-lower-shriek/def-sfb-finite-extension-by-zero-adjunction.md",
  "place": "node def-sfb-finite-extension-by-zero-adjunction, order 1655"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-sfb-finite-extension-by-zero",
  "def-sfb-finite-upper-star"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The localization functor $\\ell$ is continuous and cocontinuous, so restriction along it,\n$G\\mapsto G\\circ\\ell^{\\mathrm{op}}$, is a functor $j^{-1}$ on sheaves. As for\n[def-sfb-finite-upper-lower-star-adjunction], $j_!=\\operatorname{sheafify}\\circ\n\\operatorname{Lan}_{\\ell^{\\mathrm{op}}}$ is left adjoint to $j^{-1}$. Since $j$ is weakly\nétale, $\\ell$ is left adjoint to base change along $j$, and this induces an adjunction\n$j^{-1}\\dashv j_*$, with $j_*$ as in [def-sfb-finite-lower-star]. Both $j^{-1}$ and $j^*$\nare then left adjoint to $j_*$ ([def-sfb-finite-upper-lower-star-adjunction]), so\n$j^*\\cong j^{-1}$, and $j_!\\dashv j^{-1}\\cong j^*$.",
   "uses": [
    "def-sfb-finite-upper-lower-star-adjunction",
    "def-sfb-finite-lower-star"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
